---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Blink from '../components/Blink.astro';
import SubstackEmbed from '../components/SubstackEmbed.astro';
import { LAB_URL } from '../lib/field-briefs';

const REQUEST_URL = 'mailto:info@theairuntime.com?subject=FDE%20Circle';

const seats = [
  'Forward deployed engineers',
  'Solutions architects who own delivery',
  'Consultants and in-house deployment teams',
  'Applied AI engineers shipping to real users',
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="FDE Circle · The AI Runtime"
  description="An invite-only dinner in Boston for forward deployed engineers: the people who take AI systems from demo to deployment. Small circle, real conversation, no stage."
>
  <Section eyebrow="FDE Circle">
    <div class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="tag">Invite only</span>
        <h1>A circle of forward deployed engineers</h1>
        <p class="lede dim">
          An invite-only dinner in Boston for the people who take AI systems from demo to
          deployment. No stage, no slides, no pitch. One table, one conversation, and the war
          stories that never make it into a talk. Dinner, among people who have shipped.
        </p>
        <p class="ctas">
          <a class="btn" href={REQUEST_URL}>Ask for a seat</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/events">See all events</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="art"><Blink size={140} showMotion={true} showCheeks={true} /></div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="What it is" title="Dinner, not a meetup">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The Boston meetup is public and built around talks. The Field Lab is public and built
        around code. The FDE Circle is neither. It is a small dinner, off the record, where forward
        deployed practitioners compare notes on the work that usually stays behind an NDA: what
        broke in the client environment, where the model belonged and where it did not, what the
        customer actually accepted, and what it cost to get there.
      </p>
      <p>
        The circle stays small by design. It only works when everyone in it has shipped something
        and can say what really happened.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Who's in the circle" title="Forward deployed, whatever your title says">
    <ul class="seats">
      {seats.map((s) => (
        <li><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> {s}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="dim wide note">
      The common thread is delivery: you are accountable for an AI system working in someone
      else's environment, under their constraints.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="How to get a seat" title="Ask, and tell us what you are shipping">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        There is no public RSVP. Email us a line about what you are deploying and where, and we
        will add you to the list. Invites go out ahead of time with the date and venue.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn" href={REQUEST_URL}>Ask for a seat</a></p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Also from the FDE side" title="Talks, circles, and labs">
    <div class="related">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="arm-k">Listen</span>
        <h3>FDE Talks</h3>
        <p class="dim">
          The podcast on forward deployed AI engineering: conversations with the people who take AI
          systems from demo to deployment.
        </p>
        <a class="arm-link" href="https://theairuntime.com/s/fde-talks">Listen to FDE Talks →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="arm-k">Build</span>
        <h3>The FDE Lab</h3>
        <p class="dim">
          A public client for forward deployed work: realistic briefs, open labels, deterministic
          evaluators, and reference builds documented failure by failure.
        </p>
        <a class="arm-link" href={`${LAB_URL}/`}>Explore the FDE Lab →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Subscribe" title="Hear about the next one">
    <p class="dim wide">
      Invites go to the list first. Subscribers get the events, the recaps, and the production
      lessons behind them.
    </p>
    <SubstackEmbed
      source="fde-circle"
      headline="The AI Runtime newsletter"
      subhead="Production lessons from AI practitioners. New issues every week."
    />
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .art { order: -1; } }
  .hero h1 { margin-top: 0.6rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; max-width: 38rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .ctas { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .art { display: flex; justify-content: center; }

  .prose { max-width: 42rem; }
  .prose p { color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .seats { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; max-width: 42rem; }
  .seats li { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: baseline; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.6; }
  .seats .check { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .note { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .wide { max-width: 42rem; }

  .related { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .related { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .card {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: border-color 140ms ease;
  }
  .card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .arm-k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .card h3 { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .card p { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .arm-link { margin-top: auto; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--accent); }
</style>
